      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a fair point.\n\nHowever, it would be a misconfiguration to try to do that, and probably worth flagging...\n\nThat said, I don\u0027t see any cases where that would happen:\n\n//system/core/rootdir/init.rc\n\n# \"tcp_default_init_rwnd\" Is too long!\non property:sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd\u003d*\n    write /proc/sys/net/ipv4/tcp_default_init_rwnd ${sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd}\n\n(I\u0027m pretty sure the above won\u0027t care, because this stuff exists on cuttlefish, and the 5.4 kernel it uses doesn\u0027t even have the sysctl)\n\n//frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java\n\nInteger rwndValue \u003d Settings.Global.getInt(mContext.getContentResolver(),\n    Settings.Global.TCP_DEFAULT_INIT_RWND,\n            mSystemProperties.getInt(\"net.tcp.default_init_rwnd\", 0));\nfinal String sysctlKey \u003d \"sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd\";\nif (rwndValue !\u003d 0) {\n    mSystemProperties.set(sysctlKey, rwndValue.toString());\n}\n\n$ for i in ...; do echo; echo $i; adb -s $i shell getprop | egrep tcp | egrep init_rwnd; done\n\ntaimen[4.4]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n[sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\ncrosshatch[4.9]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\nblueline[4.9]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n[sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\nbonito[4.9]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n[sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\nf[4.14]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n[sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\naosp_cf_x86_64_phone[5.4]\n[net.tcp.default_init_rwnd]: [60]\n[sys.sysctl.tcp_def_init_rwnd]: [60]\n\n/kernel/tests/net/test/sock_diag_test.py also writes 60",
